From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] main: read the system bmon.conf from all three UAPI paths
Source: no upstream commit; written for Nex against bmon 4.0
Upstream: not submitted. bmon reads one system file at SYSCONFDIR/bmon.conf,
 so a distribution cannot ship a default that a boot or an administrator may
 replace. The change below adds the generic /usr/lib and /run tiers ahead of
 that file, keeps the existing user file after those, and names no Nex path.

At startup, when no -f configfile is given, bmon reads SYSCONFDIR/bmon.conf
and then ~/.bmonrc. There is no vendor or runtime tier, so a distribution
cannot ship a default configuration below /usr, and a running system cannot
install a temporary override below /run: only a persistent /etc file works.

Read /usr/lib/bmon/bmon.conf, then /run/bmon.conf, then the existing
SYSCONFDIR/bmon.conf, before the user file. conf_read() already overlays
each file it can read onto the config parsed so far and silently skips a
missing file, so this only adds two more optional overlay reads: an
administrator file still overrides a runtime file, which still overrides a
vendor file, which still overrides nothing. -f still replaces all three
system files with the one path given.

diff -urN a/src/conf.c b/src/conf.c
--- a/src/conf.c
+++ b/src/conf.c
@@ -605,6 +605,8 @@ void configfile_read(void)
 	if (configfile)
 		conf_read(configfile, 1);
 	else {
+		conf_read("/usr/lib/bmon/bmon.conf", 0);
+		conf_read("/run/bmon.conf", 0);
 		conf_read(SYSCONFDIR "/bmon.conf", 0);
 		
 		if (getenv("HOME")) {
